ed at 48 to 110 thousand dollars  there are five more listings for other  ear procedures costing from 27,000 to  more than $150,000 or maybe you need a  procedure involving a stent  but would you be able to pick out the  one your doctors might use from this  Florida hospitals price list is it the  one listed at 5400 dollars or the one  that costs nearly nine times that what's  more Pinder says the prices aren't real  they're fanciful they're inflated  explain that so hospitals have a list  price that's very much like the  manufacturer's suggested retail price  for electronics or a list price for a  car very rarely is the hospital ever  paid that actual list price that's  because those list prices don't take  into account the huge discounts  negotiated by Medicare and private  insurers which are considered trade  secrets Pinder worries patients may be  misled about their actual out-of-pocket  costs you might find this wildly  inflated list price and decide that you  can't afford it and choose not to get  treatment  franciene Bo Tech a senior vice  president at st. Luke's believes  releasing price lists is a step in the  right direction but she also says  hospitals need to do a better job  helping patients understand that  information this is the direction health  care needs to go  if hospitals were doing what st. Luke's  is doing and offering transparency tools  patients truly would be able to do price  shopping and they would be able to  compare so there are no uniform naming  standards the other thing is we want to  compare prices between hospitals that  would be very hard to do they all call  it something different but it's not all  hopeless Jeanie Pender says there are a  few things you can do first  ask for the medical code that will help  you zero in on the actual item on the  price list ask if there are other  charges like surgical room rates or  medications or additional tests also you  can ask how much will it cost with  insurance and without ask about the cash  price you might save money and finally  if you can get everything in writing  there has to be transparency yes what in  what other part of our lives would we  buy something or get a service and not  know how much it costs the secrecy  allows for high costs it allows for  people to make profits at other peoples  expense  I know it's hard now but I hope this  transparency pushes change we have to  have knowledge about what stuff costs in  our health care  yeah it's the only way to get healthier  and to get better price any people don't  know what anything cause and then we  don't get the bill it's so darn  confusing I can't I can't I don't even  know what they're talking about yeah  it's not it doesn't even seem in English  to me and kudos to this administration's  FDA that's got God was mandating that  drug prices be advertised on commercials  as well so again once once again  promoting transparency more consumers I  was going to say we need to send your  report to somebody yeah it's really good  obviously you always do the best report  yeah no really hopefully this will help  some people with some tips  keep it coming thank you very good thank  you
 

